  "situation": "In late 1979, US intelligence analysts were assessing the likelihood and scale of Soviet military intervention in Afghanistan. Reports recorded elevated readiness among Soviet military units over preceding months, partial mobilization near the Afghan border in late November, and additional combat units entering Afghanistan in early December. The Kabul regime was increasingly precarious, and its survival without major Soviet military support was increasingly questionable. The prevailing estimate treated limited, incremental action as most likely and judged insertion of Soviet combat forces doubtful. The reported preparations and political developments were included in daily intelligence reporting.",
